WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:04.680
The Avengers assembled once again&nbsp;
to show their support for Jeremy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.260
Renner after his recent life-threatening accident.

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:12.360
Any day is a good day to show "Avengers"&nbsp;
star Jeremy Renner love, but right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.320
in particular, he and his family&nbsp;
really need it. That's because,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:21.420
on Monday, January 2nd, Renner suffered&nbsp;
injuries related to a snowplow accident,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:26.280
sending him to the hospital in critical&nbsp;
condition and requiring two surgeries.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.760
Fortunately, the surgeries&nbsp;
appear to have gone well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:33.900
with his condition now described as&nbsp;
"critical but stable." On Tuesday,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:39.300
January 3rd, Renner made an Instagram post&nbsp;
showing himself in his hospital bed, writing,

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.700
"Oh, he's flatlining. Call it. Time?"

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:52.080
"No, no, no, I'm gonna live forever.&nbsp;
I'm gonna be made of plastic!"

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:58.200
The accident occurred after Renner attempted to&nbsp;
use his snowplow to clear a path for a family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:03.000
member's trapped vehicle. He stepped outside&nbsp;
the vehicle to talk to the family member,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.320
at which point the snowplow started to&nbsp;
move on its own. Renner tried to jump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:12.720
into the vehicle to stop it but instead was&nbsp;
run over, causing multiple serious injuries.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:18.060
The beloved actor's Instagram has&nbsp;
over 5 million likes and over 200,000&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:22.200
comments, most of which are expressing&nbsp;
their love for Renner and wishing him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:27.000
a quick recovery. However, it's not just&nbsp;
common fans expressing their best wishes.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:31.260
Among the hundreds of thousands of&nbsp;
comments wishing Jeremy Renner well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:35.100
were those who have starred alongside&nbsp;
him in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:38.520
Renner plays Clint Barton, also known as Hawkeye.

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.120
Chris Hemsworth, who plays&nbsp;
Thor in the MCU commented,

00:01:45.679 --> 00:01:49.920
Hemsworth is not the only Chris from&nbsp;
the MCU sending his love to the actor.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:54.120
Chris Pratt, who plays Peter&nbsp;
Quill, also known as Star-Lord,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:59.100
in the "Guardians of the Galaxy" and "Avengers"&nbsp;
films, commented on Renner's post, writing,

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:07.920
But there was still one more Chris to send some&nbsp;
love Renner's way. Chris Evans, who plays Steve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:13.140
Rogers in the "Captain America" and "Avengers"&nbsp;
films, also had kind words. Evans wrote,

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.840
Beyond actors named Chris, Paul Bettany,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:22.320
who plays Vision in "WandaVision"&nbsp;
and the "Avengers" films, wrote,

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:28.607
Josh Brolin, who plays the&nbsp;
villainous Thanos, wrote,

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:39.120
Alaqua Cox, who plays Echo, in "Hawkeye" and&nbsp;
the upcoming Disney+ series "Echo," also took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:43.380
to Instagram to send Renner her love,&nbsp;
simply commenting with two heart emojis.

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:46.920
Finally, Mark Ruffalo, who plays Bruce Banner and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:50.515
his alter ego the Hulk wrote&nbsp;
on his own Instagram account,

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:02.340
It's not only Jeremy Renner's fellow actors&nbsp;
from the MCU who are sending him their love,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:07.500
however. Many of the various directors of&nbsp;
the MCU's films have also taken to the star's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:11.880
comment section to show him they're thinking of&nbsp;
him and wishing him the best in his recovery.

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:16.260
Taika Waititi, director of&nbsp;
"Thor: Ragnarök" and "Thor:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:20.520
Love and Thunder," commented on Renner's&nbsp;
post, writing, "My brother I love you."

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:24.000
Anthony and Joe Russo, directors of several of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:28.200
biggest films in the MCU franchise&nbsp;
also left a kind comment, writing,

00:03:32.217 --> 00:03:36.960
Last but not least, James Gunn, director&nbsp;
of the "Guardians of the Galaxy" films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:42.540
posted a single heart and an emoji of hands being&nbsp;
raised to show Renner his love and well wishes.

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:45.780
As terrible of a situation&nbsp;
the beloved actor is in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:49.980
he at least won't want for kind messages&nbsp;
from his fans and co-workers alike.

